Wrapping the quick filter buttons in `.filter-btn-cell` breaks the mobile layout grid. On mobile (screens ≤ 640px), `.filter-btn` has `flex: 1 1 calc(33.333% - 2px)` to form a 3-column grid. However, because `.filter-btn-cell` is now the direct child of the `.filter-buttons` flex container, the flex properties must be applied to `.filter-btn-cell` instead of `.filter-btn` on mobile. Otherwise, the cells will shrink to their content size and align to the right, completely breaking the responsive grid.

To fix this, update the mobile media query (`@media (max-width: 640px)`) to apply the flex basis to `.filter-btn-cell` and make `.filter-btn` span the full width of its cell:

```css
.filter-btn-cell {
  flex: 1 1 calc(33.333% - 2px);
  min-width: 0;
}
.filter-btn {
  width: 100%;
}
```

